In plain words: churches, schools and anyone else may use and share this app
freely, as it is, provided that

  • Attribution — Faith Baptist Church of Plymouth County is named as its
    maker, with a link to https://fbckjv.app/KJVBible, and its name, logo and
    footer are left in place;
  • NonCommercial — it is not sold, charged for, or used to make money; and
  • NoDerivatives — it is not changed, rebranded, or passed off as someone
    else's work.

To ask about anything beyond this, write to the church from the app
(Settings → About → Write to the church).

“Freely ye have received, freely give.” — Matthew 10:8

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Works by others that the app includes

These keep their own terms; the licence above does not cover them.

  • The King James Bible text — public domain.
  • Webster's American Dictionary of the English Language (1828) — public
    domain; the transcription in dictionary/ is by akaitsurugi/webster1828
    under CC BY-SA 4.0, and those files stay under CC BY-SA 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  • Strong's Exhaustive Concordance (James Strong, 1890) — public domain; XML
    by David Troidl, David Instone-Brewer and Ulrik Petersen.
  • Hitchcock's Bible Names Dictionary (1869) — public domain, compiled via the
    BibleData project.
  • The Treasury of Scripture Knowledge — public domain, as arranged by
    CrossReferences.org, CC BY 4.0.
  • Bible places — OpenBible.info geocoding data, CC BY 4.0.
  • Bible people and Nave's Topical Bible (1896, public domain) — digitized
    by BibleData (Brady Stephenson), CC BY 4.0.
  • Hymn words — published before 1928 and in the public domain; sources are
    noted in tools/hymns/texts.json.
  • The classic map plates, the audio Bible recordings, and any other images
    or recordings made by others keep the terms their makers set.

Their credits are also shown in the app, in each tool and under Settings → About.
